# Mobile App Environment Configuration
# Copy this file to .env and fill in the values.
# NEVER commit the .env file to version control - it contains secrets!
# $ cp .env.example .env

# --- API Configuration ---
# The URL of your Quark web app backend (no trailing slash)
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:3000

# --- Google OAuth (Optional) ---
# Get credentials at: https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials
# EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your_google_client_id
#
# This must be the SAME client id the web app has as GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID. The
# server compares it against the token's audience on every sign-in, so a
# mismatch here fails the login with an "invalid token" error.

# --- Apple Sign In (Optional) ---
# Apple Sign In is configured via EAS and Apple Developer Console.
# No environment variables needed - it uses native module configuration.
#
# The web app must have APPLE_CLIENT_ID set, or POST /api/auth/apple
# refuses every request as unconfigured. It takes a comma-separated
# list of audiences, and native iOS identity tokens carry the bundle
# identifier from app.json as their audience (the Services ID applies
# to web-flow tokens only) - so include the bundle identifier here, or
# every native sign-in fails with 401.
